{"availability":"available","full":"NOC-OBG-Autonomy/pelagos-py","name":"pelagos-py","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":12,"forks":12,"created":"2025-03-10T16:02:30Z","updated":"2026-10-16T12:57:32Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://noc-obg-autonomy.github.io/pelagos-py/","topics":[],"demo":"https://noc-obg-autonomy.github.io/pelagos-py/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:32.146Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:32.146Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:32.146Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:39:36.224Z","stars":12,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-13T02:09:27.969Z","stars":12,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-19T02:46:32.146Z","stars":12,"forks":12}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pelagos-py provides a flexible, modular pipeline framework for defining, executing, and visualising multi-step data-processing workflows for oceanographic data.","Each pipeline is composed of a series of steps that are automatically built from a central user-defined YAML configuration file. As Pelagos-py only depends on the config file to construct a pipeline, processing can be easily reproduced by others through sharing of configs.","The Pipeline class orchestrates the flow of data through a sequence of modular \"steps.\" Each step performs a specific processing task (e.g., data loading, quality control, profile detection, export)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NOC-OBG-Autonomy/pelagos-py/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0a062acfa508e69d19442429c5ee281d9f0927fab60d49e5fd58b32930d8294e","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:36.393Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:36.393Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Pelagos-py provides a flexible, modular pipeline framework for defining, executing, and visualising multi-step data-processing workflows for oceanographic data.","sourceUrl":"https:/